    "fullText": "On September 12, 2025, the FAA proposed $3,139,319 in civil penalties against Boeing, using its maximum statutory authority. The violations ran from September 2023 through February 2024. The FAA found hundreds of quality system violations at Boeing's 737 factory in Renton and at Spirit AeroSystems' 737 factory in Wichita, and Boeing presented two unairworthy aircraft for airworthiness certificates.\n\nIt also found that a Boeing employee outside the ODA pressured an ODA unit member to sign off a 737 MAX so Boeing could meet its delivery schedule, after the member had found the aircraft did not comply. Since the 2020 law, that kind of pressure is unlawful.",
