    "kicker": "Apply the lesson: what does a fixed-price bet cost when it goes wrong?",
    "fullText": "In July 2025, Lockheed Martin reported $1.6 billion in program losses for the second quarter. The largest was $950 million on a classified, fixed-price aeronautics program, on top of $555 million on the same program in the fourth quarter of 2024. It also took $570 million on the Canadian Maritime Helicopter program and $95 million on the Turkish Utility Helicopter program, both linked to customers restructuring those programs.\n\nCEO Jim Taiclet called the classified program a game-changing capability and said Lockheed expected to keep reducing its risk over the next few years. On a fixed price, that risk is the company's to carry.",
